==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|zwō|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} *''tw(a)ōz'' (see {{m|gem-pro|*twai}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}}. ''Zwō'' is originally the feminine form, but is now used as a variant of {{term|zwei|lang=de}} without gender distinction. Compare, however, {{etym|lb|-}} {{term|zwou|lang=lb}}, which is still a feminine form of {{term|zwéin|lang=lb}}. More at ''[[two]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tsvoː/|lang=de}}

===Numeral===
{{head|de|numeral}}

# [[two]]

====Usage notes====
* {{term|zwei|Zwei|lang=de}} is the usual German word for "two", but {{term||zwo|lang=de}} is sometimes used as more clearly distinguishable from {{term|drei||three|lang=de}}, especially over the telephone and in military parlance. Otherwise, it is used more in southern Germany and Austria.

